+config ARM64_MEMORY_MODEL_CONTROL
+	bool "Per-thread memory model control (x86 TSO for emulators)"
+	help
+	  Apple's CPUs can run a thread under x86's total store order
+	  (TSO), which an x86 emulator otherwise has to build out of
+	  ordered loads and stores. With this option a thread asks for it
+	  with prctl(PR_SET_MEM_MODEL, PR_SET_MEM_MODEL_TSO); it is
+	  inherited by fork and clone and reset by exec. The mode is bit 1
+	  of ACTLR_EL1, offered where AIDR_EL1 bit 9 is set on an Apple
+	  implementer, as Hypervisor.framework offers it to a guest.
 
+	  Under a hypervisor every access to ACTLR_EL1 traps, so the
+	  register is written at a context switch only when the next
+	  thread's mode differs from what the CPU holds, and never read
+	  there.
+
 menu "ARMv8.1 architectural features"
 
 config ARM64_HW_AFDBM
